{
  "item": {
    "id": "c16237dd-cbed-4c2b-b0d3-04cfee06cebb",
    "content_type": "generic",
    "workflow_state": "public",
    "page_title": "Rate limits",
    "short_description": "Rate limits by plan tier, rate limit headers, and pagination envelope for the Godzilla API (v2 and v3 endpoints).",
    "body": "<h1>Rate limits {{ds:component/chip|label=v2 / v3|variant=primary}} {{ds:component/chip|label=Stable|variant=success}}</h1>

{{ds:component/stat|value=100|label=requests / minute (Starter)|description=Rate limit for Starter-tier API keys, per workspace.}}
{{ds:component/stat|value=1,000|label=requests / minute (Standard)|description=Default rate limit for Standard-tier API keys, per workspace.}}
{{ds:component/stat|value=10,000+|label=requests / minute (Enterprise)|description=Custom rate limit for Enterprise-tier API keys, per workspace.}}

<h2 id="headers">Rate limit headers</h2>
<p>Every response includes <code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code>, <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code>, and <code>X-RateLimit-Reset</code>. A request over the limit returns <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with a <code>Retry-After</code> header.</p>
<p>To view limits across all plan tiers or what happens when an account exceeds its quota, see the <a href="{{cms:item/d97f17dc-e9d7-4308-929b-db9f2e159f5d}}">Quotas &amp; billing</a> reference.</p>

<h2 id="pagination">Pagination</h2>
<p>List endpoints (<a href="{{cms:item/18937bd0-7c49-4484-9f01-63bf86de09e3}}">Pipelines</a>, <a href="{{cms:item/cac7ba67-fc6d-4db4-81ef-efdeef87c39e}}">Connectors</a>, <a href="{{cms:item/8c783686-5f91-4b49-baaf-f1fea642630a}}">Events</a>) use cursor-based pagination — a departure from v1's offset-based pagination.</p>

